696:
Upon receipt of an application for a license in accordance with the provisions of section 10.4.5 and a check for $25.00 to cover the investigation fee, the chief of police shall cause such investigation of the applicant's business responsibility or moral character to be made as he deems necessary for the protection of the public good. The chief of police shall make a report of his investigation to the city administrator. The chief of police may, after investigation and finding that the health, safety, or welfare of the public so demands, recommend that a license not be issued to an applicant for reasons including, but not limited to, the following:
(a) Conviction of any felony under the laws of this state or any other state of the United States, provided, however, this shall not apply to any person who has been convicted of a felony after ten (10) years have expired from the date of completion of the felony sentence;
(b) Conviction of any crime within the ten (10) years immediately preceding the date of the filing of the application involving moral turpitude;
(c) Fraud, misrepresentation or false statement of material or relevant facts contained in the application;
(d) That the applicant has engaged in a fraudulent transaction or enterprise; or
(e) An applicant for a license may, in the discretion of the city administrator be issued a temporary permit based upon a preliminary investigation by the chief of police, which permit shall remain in effect until the issuance or denial of a license as herein provided. A confidential record of the investigation shall be kept on file by the chief of police.
The license issued hereunder shall be a personal privilege and shall not be transferable, nor shall there be any abatement of the license fee for such license by reason of the fact that the license holder shall have exercised the privilege for any period of less than it was granted. The license fee for an established dealer is $300.00.
The issuance of a license to any itinerant dealer shall specify the place and date or dates upon which the business may be conducted. A license fee of $10.00 per day shall be charged, and the license shall be issued only for the period specified in the application.
The license issued under this article shall be posted conspicuously in each place of business named therein. Each person receiving such license shall place over the principal entrance of his place of business a sign designating that he is a licensed dealer.
(2010-10-15, § 3, Amended, 10/11/2010)

