Any owner and occupants of a short-term rental who obtains a business license under this article shall comply with the following:
(a) All short-term rentals shall comply with all City of Roswell ordinances regarding water, and sanitation services;
(b) All short-term rentals shall have an owner or agent available twenty-four (24) hours per day on days the property is occupied by guest;
(c) All taxes and administrative fees must be timely paid;
(d) All noise restrictions of the City of Roswell;
(e) Occupancy of such short-term rental shall comply with all other life safety, health and sanitation regulations and building code, ordinances and/or regulations of the City of Roswell, Fulton County, and the State of Georgia;
(f) Occupancy limits of all short-term rental units shall be limited to standards contained in NFPA 101 as may be amended from time and all advertising shall include notification of such occupancy limits;
(g) A copy of the occupational tax certificate shall be posted at all times within the unit.
(h) All short-term rentals shall have full inspections by the Roswell fire marshal prior to being offered to the public for lodging or use and annually as required thereafter.
